# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy this file to .env.local and uncomment lines you need to override.
# Never commit .env.local to source control.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ── MongoDB (required for shared, persistent storage on Vercel) ──────────────
#
# Without this the built-in /api routes fall back to an in-memory store that
# resets on every cold start and is NOT shared across users.
#
# Setup:
#   1. Create a free cluster at https://mongodb.com/atlas
#   2. Database Access → add a user with readWrite on your database
#   3. Network Access → allow 0.0.0.0/0 (Vercel IPs are dynamic)
#   4. Connect → Drivers → copy the connection string
#   5. Append your database name, e.g.:
#        mongodb+srv://<user>:<password>@cluster0.xxx.mongodb.net/taskflow
#   6. Add as MONGODB_URI in Vercel → Settings → Environment Variables
#      Do NOT use the NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix — this key must stay server-only.
#
# MONGODB_URI=mongodb+srv://<user>:<password>@cluster0.xxx.mongodb.net/taskflow
